wxt5x0
Copyright 2017-2024 Matthew Wall
Distributed under terms of the GPLv3

This is a driver for weeWX that collects data from Vaisala WXT5x0 hardware.

===============================================================================
Installation

1) install the the driver

  weectl extension install https://github.com/matthewwall/weewx-wxt5x0/archive/master.zip

2) configure weeWX to use the driver

  weectl station reconfigure

3) restart weeWX

  sudo systemctl restart weewx

Independent continuation (0.9.0)

This repository continues matthewwall/weewx-wxt5x0 with original history and
GPL-3.0-only licensing. TCP serial-server support follows the use case in
OH2LAK's PR #12. Connections open during polling and reconnect after EOF or
socket errors. A failed connection does not abort driver construction.

Install and select the driver explicitly with the station's configuration file:

    weectl extension install https://github.com/weewx-packages/weewx-wxt5x0/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.0.zip
    weectl station reconfigure --driver=user.wxt5x0 --config=/path/to/weewx.conf

To connect a serial server, use these options in [WXT5x0]:

    protocol = tcp
    tcp_address = 192.168.1.20
    tcp_port = 5000
    address = 0

The server must expose raw ASCII serial data. After max_tries, the driver raises
RetriesExceeded so WeeWX can restart its engine and try again.

Rain accumulation requires Rc, the cumulative rain counter. Ri is a rate and Rp
is a peak rate. They cannot replace Rc. Configure the transmitter to include Rc
in composite responses. Rc and Ri can be verified independently in the fixture
tests using `python -m pytest -q tests`.

Tests cover local TCP disconnection/reconnection and serial parsing. Confirm
counter configuration and telemetry recovery on the actual transmitter.
